  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "Machine A produces \\(3/5\\) of the products and has a defect rate of \\(1/10\\); machine B produces \\(2/5\\) and has a defect rate of \\(1/5\\). Given that 1 selected item is defective, what is the probability that it came from A?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "3/7",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Given a defect, the required probability is A's defective contribution divided by the total defect probability. The numerator is \\((3/5)(1/10)=3/50\\), and the denominator adds the disjoint contributions from both machines: \\(3/50+(2/5)(1/5)=7/50>0\\). Thus the conditional probability is\n\\[\n\\frac{3/50}{7/50}=\\frac37.\n\\]",
